  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moldova: Advancing Integrity and Transparency for a Modern Justice Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To enhance capacity of the Ministry of Justice of Moldova to lead digital transformation efforts. 2) To increase accessibility and transparency in bankruptcy and insolvency proceedings. 3) To enhance capacity of the National Institute of Justice to develop the next generation of civil servants resilient to corruption. 4) To advance corruption reporting through public awareness and inclusive digital solutions. 5) To improve digital capabilities of the National Integrity Authority to process and analyze declarations of public officials.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Ministry of Justice, National Institute of Justice, National Integrity Authority, Union of Authorized Administrators, National Anti-Corruption Centre. Indirect beneficiaries: Moldovan population at large.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to reduce corruption and strengthen civic engagement with justice sector institutions in the Republic of Moldova by leveraging digital technologies to enhance the transparency and efficiency of the justice sector, contributing to advancing integrity and accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
